WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:07.120
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am going&nbsp;
to explain an Indian psychological drama film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:15.920
called “Taare Zameen Par.” Spoilers&nbsp;
ahead! Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:21.840
Ishaan is an eight-year-old imaginative kid,&nbsp;
widely known as a troublemaker among his mates.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:26.080
He fails every subject and is the&nbsp;
lowest-ranking student in his classroom.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:31.200
He is in his second year of third grade and by the&nbsp;
looks of his report card, he will have to repeat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:37.440
the same grade again. In contrast to Ishaan,&nbsp;
his elder brother Yohaan is an ideal student.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:43.360
Outside studies, he plays tennis and is competing&nbsp;
in the upcoming inter-state tennis championship.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:48.160
Ishaan frequently gets into fights with the&nbsp;
neighborhood kids who bully him. One day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:53.200
a kid’s mother complains about Ishaan’s&nbsp;
behavior to his father Nandkishore. He has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:58.640
to embarrassingly apologize to the kid and his&nbsp;
mother. After they leave, he shoves Ishaan to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:04.720
the floor to discipline him. Although Nandkishore&nbsp;
loves his children, he is too harsh on Ishaan. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:09.920
believes that Ishaan’s low scores and inability&nbsp;
to do basic tasks are because of his laziness.
&nbsp;

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:14.720
The next day at school, Ishaan’s English teacher&nbsp;
asks him to read a line from the book. He tries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:19.680
his best but can hardly form a word. He has&nbsp;
difficulty in understanding the letters but the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:25.840
teachers mistake it for him being a brat. When she&nbsp;
repeatedly urges him to read, he yells gibberish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.960
and is sent out of the class. It is not a&nbsp;
new thing for Ishaan to be punished. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:39.760
he spends most of his time outside rather than&nbsp;
studying because the teachers think of him as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:44.880
a disturbance to the other students. That&nbsp;
day, Ishaan hadn't done his math homework.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.760
To avoid facing the math teacher, he runs&nbsp;
away from school and spends the entire day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:53.200
wandering around the neighborhood.
He enjoys the day to his fullest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:58.800
buying ice cream, spending time by the sea, and&nbsp;
analyzing the passersby. By the end of the day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:03.200
he returns to his school bus without&nbsp;
anyone noticing his absence. At home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:08.640
we see him make a beautiful painting. Ishaan&nbsp;
loves to paint and his imaginative mind helps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:14.320
the cause resulting in over-the-top pieces.&nbsp;
Later, his mother Maya tries to tutor him and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:19.280
make him do his homework. She notices that his&nbsp;
handwriting is awful and he can hardly spell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:25.120
anything right. She associates his inability with&nbsp;
laziness and scolds him like everyone else. 
&nbsp;

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:29.760
The next day, Ishaan will have to provide his&nbsp;
teacher with an absent note from his parents.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:33.360
Scared of getting in trouble, he begs&nbsp;
his brother to write the note for him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:38.800
Yohaan makes him promise he will never skip school&nbsp;
again and writes the note. The kid shows it to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:43.600
teacher who doesn’t question its authenticity.&nbsp;
He also pretends to cough to make it seem like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:49.360
he was actually sick. That day, the math teacher&nbsp;
surprises the kids with a test. Ishaan is handed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:54.560
the test paper but to him, the letters look like&nbsp;
they are dancing. The first question asks him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:59.520
the multiplication of three with nine. In his&nbsp;
head, the kid imagines the third planet Earth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:05.520
and the ninth “planet” Pluto fighting each other.&nbsp;
He fantasizes about the Earth destroying Pluto and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:11.040
rationalizes that the answer is three. Leaving&nbsp;
the rest of the questions blank, he submits the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:16.560
test. When asked by his friends, he confidently&nbsp;
claims that he enjoyed the test thoroughly.
&nbsp;

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:21.120
The next day, Nandkishore returns from a&nbsp;
business trip. Ishaan is overjoyed by his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:26.560
father’s return and hugs him dearly. However,&nbsp;
during breakfast, Nandkishore finds the fake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:32.080
absent note from the day before. On investigating,&nbsp;
he finds out about Ishaan running away from school&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:37.360
and wandering alone in the streets. The very next&nbsp;
day, the parents go to meet his teachers and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:42.800
principal who condemn his behavior in class. They&nbsp;
also find out about the recent math test and its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:47.920
results. The principal assumes Ishaan is a special&nbsp;
child who needs to be sent to school for children&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:52.800
with disabilities. Nandkishore is horrified&nbsp;
at the thought of his son being disabled.
&nbsp;

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:57.200
Both parents are worried about their kid’s future&nbsp;
so they decide to send him to a boarding school.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:01.920
Ishaan is completely against the idea.&nbsp;
He rebels and cries, begging them to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:06.080
keep him home and although the parents do&nbsp;
not want to be separated from him either,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:10.960
they do what they think will be the best for him.&nbsp;
That night, Ishaan dreams of losing his mother in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:16.160
a crowd and wakes up screaming. When she tries&nbsp;
to calm him down, he promises to study harder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:22.000
if they let him be home. This breaks Maya’s heart&nbsp;
but Nandkishore is adamant about his decision. 
&nbsp;

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:26.000
The day finally comes when Ishaan is taken to&nbsp;
the boarding school in the countryside. He will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:31.120
have to share a dorm with other children and will&nbsp;
only be allowed to meet his family once a month.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:35.600
It is a nightmare for the eight-year-old who&nbsp;
has never been away from his home. The hostel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:41.200
warden welcomes him by declaring that his old ways&nbsp;
won’t be tolerated here. After touring the school,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:47.200
the family leaves with a heavy heart. Ishaan just&nbsp;
watches their car drive away with teary eyes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:51.600
He stays like that for several minutes even&nbsp;
after the car vanishes from his view.
&nbsp;

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:56.320
When it starts to get dark, he walks inside the&nbsp;
hostel while still crying. He doesn’t talk to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.320 --> 00:05:01.120
anyone and hardly eats dinner. At night, when&nbsp;
he cannot sleep he goes to the bathroom and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:06.960
cries quietly, missing his mother. Meanwhile, Maya&nbsp;
reaches home and goes through Ishaan’s belongings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:12.560
To her dismay, she finds a flipbook of him&nbsp;
being taken away from his family. The book&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:16.800
breaks her heart as she realizes how much&nbsp;
the kid dreads being away from them. 
&nbsp;

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:25.200
In the hostel, Ishaan struggles to do normal&nbsp;
things like tying his tie and shoelaces. On&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:30.640
his first day, the Hindi teacher Mr. Tiwari makes&nbsp;
him sit on the first bench with the class topper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:35.600
Rajan. The teachers soon realize that Ishaan&nbsp;
isn’t normal. He hardly pays attention in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:40.160
class and is physically punished by his&nbsp;
art teacher. Nothing changes from how he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:45.120
was in the previous school. He is always sent&nbsp;
outside the class as punishment and is excluded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:50.160
from the class activity for ruining it. 
With time, he gets so frustrated that he tears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:55.040
his books apart and throws them into the bin.&nbsp;
He stops trying to do better in school and goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.040 --> 00:06:00.160
into a spiral of depression and self-loathing.&nbsp;
When his parents come to meet him after a month,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:05.600
he locks himself inside a room and bursts out&nbsp;
crying for the first time since he last saw them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:10.560
On being urged, he runs outside and takes&nbsp;
several laps of the basketball court to rebel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:14.960
The family takes him to a hotel for the night&nbsp;
to give him a break from his life at the hostel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:20.240
Yohaan gives him a hamper of painting supplies&nbsp;
as a gift but little does he know, Ishaan has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:25.600
shut out his creative side and stopped painting&nbsp;
altogether. The next day, the family bids him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:31.040
farewell and leaves him alone yet again. 
Later that day, Ishaan is the lowest he has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:35.280
ever been. He looks down from the terrace&nbsp;
of the school thinking about how it feels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:40.640
to jump from that height. His only friend Rajan&nbsp;
interrupts his thoughts and tells him about their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:46.000
new art teacher. Ishaan doesn’t think much of it&nbsp;
because no teacher has ever helped him. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:51.600
it is surprising to the kids that the new teacher&nbsp;
Ram enters the class in a joker costume. He sings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:57.520
a song, plays flute, makes them dance, and lets&nbsp;
them enjoy the class, in contrast to all other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:02.400
teachers. While the old Ishaan would have loved&nbsp;
this, the depressed one doesn’t participate in any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:08.000
of it. As their first task, the students are asked&nbsp;
to draw or paint anything they want. Ram wants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:12.720
them to show their creative side so he knows what&nbsp;
he has to work on next. The children start to draw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:17.360
several things, all different from one another’s,&nbsp;
but Ishaan doesn’t even touch the paper.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:22.000
Initially, Ram assumes that the kid is taking&nbsp;
some time to think but even when the class ends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:27.280
Ishaan’s paper is blank. Worried, Ram asks&nbsp;
him what is wrong but doesn’t get a reply. 
&nbsp;

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:32.720
That evening, Maya calls to talk to Ishaan&nbsp;
but he only holds the phone to his ears and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:37.200
doesn’t say anything. He is informed that they&nbsp;
will have to postpone the next visit by a week&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:42.480
because of Yohaan’s tennis competition. To Ishaan,&nbsp;
this only confirms that his family doesn’t care&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:48.400
about him. He sheds a single tear and walks away&nbsp;
without saying anything. The next day, Ram sees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:53.040
Ishaan kneeling down outside the classroom.&nbsp;
Intrigued by his behavior, he asks Rajan about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:58.720
him. Rajan reveals that Ishaan has difficulty&nbsp;
understanding letters no matter how hard he tries.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:03.760
Ram teaches in a school for disabled children so&nbsp;
he has an eye for kids who are special. To find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:08.800
out more about Ishaan, he goes through his old&nbsp;
notebooks and finds a pattern of similar mistakes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:12.640
Even while teaching the special children,&nbsp;
he cannot get the thought of Ishaan out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:17.920
his head. He used to have the same problem in his&nbsp;
childhood so he feels sympathetic to the kid. 
&nbsp;

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:23.040
Weeks later, he recognizes what Ishaan’s actual&nbsp;
problem is and travels to his hometown to meet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:27.680
his parents. They welcome him and let him take&nbsp;
a look at Ishaan’s bedroom. Ram is surprised to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:32.560
find out that Ishaan used to paint. This makes&nbsp;
him even sadder that the kid lost his sparkle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:36.640
because of the pressure that was put&nbsp;
on him. Nandkishore belittles his son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:41.280
claiming that he is lazy and hates studying.&nbsp;
Ram retaliates and shows them the pattern in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:46.880
Ishaan’s mistakes. He often inverts the letters&nbsp;
as if he has difficulty differentiating them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:51.760
Still, the father associates it with laziness&nbsp;
but Ram bluntly claims that he is wrong.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:57.120
He declares Ishaan has a neurological condition&nbsp;
called dyslexia that causes him to not understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:02.560
certain patterns like letters and words. In&nbsp;
addition, he has difficulty coordinating which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:07.360
causes him to not be able to tie his shoelace.&nbsp;
The kid must have been suffering so much because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:11.200
no one understood that he couldn’t read&nbsp;
and assumed he was just being lazy. 
&nbsp;

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:21.600
Nandkishore thinks Ram is calling his son a retard&nbsp;
and lashes out at him. To make him understand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:26.080
Ram asks him to read foreign letters written&nbsp;
on a box. When Nandkishore is scolded for not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:30.640
understanding the letters, he finally realizes&nbsp;
what his kid must be going through. Still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:35.760
he refuses to acknowledge that his son can make a&nbsp;
living out of his only passion; painting. Ram is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:40.240
determined to prove him wrong. When he returns to&nbsp;
the school the next day, he teaches the kids about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:44.480
all the famous historical figures who weren’t&nbsp;
so good at studying when they were children.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:49.920
He gives them examples of scientists, actors, and&nbsp;
philosophers which makes Ishaan feel a lot better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:54.960
about himself. When Ram asks them who invented&nbsp;
the light bulb, Ishaan speaks for the first time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.960 --> 00:10:01.040
in weeks and answers, Thomas Eddison. Ram sees a&nbsp;
shimmer of hope for the boy to learn. Later that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:06.240
day, Ishaan is by the pond when he uses rubber&nbsp;
bands and leaves to make a working boat. 
&nbsp;

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:11.280
Ram is so impressed that he brings the structure&nbsp;
home and keeps it as a decoration. Ishaan’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:16.320
creative senses start to flow again but he still&nbsp;
has a long way to go before learning to study like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:21.520
the other kids his age. One day, Ram goes to the&nbsp;
school’s principal and tells him about Ishaan’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:26.000
problem. The principal suggests they send him to&nbsp;
the school for children with special needs but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:31.200
Ram is confident that Ishaan can study with the&nbsp;
regular kids. He suggests the teachers understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:35.680
the kid’s problem and help him accordingly.&nbsp;
When the principal says it is not possible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:41.840
Ram offers to teach Ishaan every day after school.&nbsp;
The principal allows it for the sake of the child.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:47.200
Starting the next day, Ram uses various innovative&nbsp;
methods to help Ishaan differentiate letters of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:53.600
the alphabet. They learn using sandboxes, play&nbsp;
dough, sensory methods, and so on. Ishaan also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:58.400
takes help from audiobooks and stairs to&nbsp;
learn to calculate. In only two months,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:03.280
he begins to understand the letters that the other&nbsp;
teachers couldn’t teach him in several years. 
&nbsp;

00:11:03.280 --> 00:11:08.400
One day, Nandkishore comes to the school to talk&nbsp;
to Ram and boast about how they are researching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:13.280
more about their son’s condition. He wants Ram&nbsp;
to know he is not an absent father and is proud&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:17.600
to be the way he is. Ram, on the other hand,&nbsp;
blames the father for being the reason the kid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:23.280
lost self-confidence which even Nandkishore&nbsp;
cannot deny. On his way out, he sees Ishaan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:28.480
trying to read from the notice board. Regretful&nbsp;
of unknowingly hurting his child, he tears up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:32.720
and cannot get himself to face him. 
A few days later, Ram organizes a painting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:37.600
competition for both teachers and the students of&nbsp;
the school. Everyone gathers in the amphitheater&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:42.320
and participates. Ishaan uses the painting&nbsp;
supplies that he was gifted by his brother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:47.360
for the first time. The competition starts and&nbsp;
everyone gets busy drawing. Even the teachers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.360 --> 00:11:52.880
enjoy the event and do their best. By the end of&nbsp;
it, Ishaan creates a beautiful painting of himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:57.280
sitting by the pond. He goes to the front to&nbsp;
submit the painting and sees that Ram has painted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:02.560
a portrait of him. He is left speechless at the&nbsp;
sight. A while later, it is announced that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:07.120
winning painting will be on the front of the new&nbsp;
edition of their yearbook. The principal proclaims&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:12.720
that the decision was difficult because two&nbsp;
paintings stood out the most; Ram’s and Ishaan’s.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:17.840
In the end, Ishaan is declared the winner while&nbsp;
the second prize goes to Ram. The crowd erupts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:23.280
in cheers. For the first time in his life, Ishaan&nbsp;
feels recognized for his talent. He cannot help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:28.720
but cry and runs to his teacher to hug him. 
In the last scene, Maya and Nandkishore come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:32.000
to the school for the end of the year&nbsp;
parent-teacher meeting. The principal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:36.480
boasts about Ishaan’s talent showing them his&nbsp;
painting on the front of the school’s yearbook.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:42.320
Unused to the new attention, the parents are left&nbsp;
shocked. The principal also praises Ram for doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:46.880
a great job teaching the kid in the way he&nbsp;
needed it. Later, the parents meet Ishaan’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:51.840
teachers who show them the report card and&nbsp;
compliment the kid’s undeniable progress. 
&nbsp;

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:57.760
Outside, the couple watches their son playing and&nbsp;
cry tears of happiness. Nandkishore thanks Ram for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.760 --> 00:13:04.720
helping Ishaan and apologizes for his behavior.&nbsp;
Lastly, Ishaan bids farewell to Ram and goes back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:09.120
to his hometown for a vacation. 
